      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "All syntheses were carried out in air in glass beakers. Ln(Tfa)3(H2O)3 (Ln = La, Nd) was first prepared from Ln2(CO3)3·6H2O by a known procedure (yield ~95%). For I, a weighed sample of La(Tfa)3(H2O)3 (0.7 mmol) was dispersed in isopropyl alcohol (5 mL), and Deta (1.4 mmol, 0.151 mL) was added with stirring. The mixture was stirred at 60 °C until a transparent solution was obtained, then cooled slowly and left in an open beaker for solvent evaporation and slow crystallization. After 3 days, few colorless crystals of I were obtained in the volume of the gel-like hydrolysis product.",
